   "answer": "Financial aid is linked to a lower re-arrest rate after adjustment (hazard ratio 0.684, 95% CI 0.47 to 0.996, p = 0.0474), but the result is borderline.\n\n| Measure | Value | 95% CI | n (what one n is) | Test | Step |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Adjusted hazard ratio, financial aid vs no aid | 0.684 | 0.47 to 0.996 | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Cox model, Efron ties, two-sided, alpha 0.05; adjusted for age, race, wexp, mar, paro, prio. Wald CI and p | fit_cox (main) |\n| Adjusted p-value, financial aid | 0.0474 | not applicable | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Same Cox model, Wald test | fit_cox (main) |\n| Sensitivity hazard ratio, stratified by wexp | 0.684 | 0.470 to 0.995 | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Cox model stratified by wexp, Efron ties; p = 0.0469 | run_script (lifelines) |\n| Unadjusted log-rank, financial aid | chi-square 3.838, p = 0.0501 | not applicable | 432 men: 216 per group; 66 re-arrests (no aid), 48 (aid) | Log-rank test, two-sided, alpha 0.05 | kaplan_meier |\n| Concordance of main model | 0.640 | not applicable | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Harrell concordance from Cox model | fit_cox (main) |\n| Proportional hazards test, financial aid | p = 0.902 (passes) | not applicable | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Schoenfeld-residual test | fit_cox (main) |\n| Proportional hazards test, age | p = 0.00071 (fails) | not applicable | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Schoenfeld-residual test | fit_cox (main) |\n| Proportional hazards test, wexp | p = 0.0068 (fails) | not applicable | 432 men, 114 re-arrests | Schoenfeld-residual test | fit_cox (main) |\n\nUncertain:\n- The aid estimate sits near alpha. The p-value is 0.0474, the upper CI limit is 0.996, and the unadjusted log-rank p is 0.0501.\n- Age and wexp break proportional hazards, so their hazard ratios are averages over time. The aid estimate stays about the same when the model stratifies by wexp. The stratified model ran in a script because the program tool failed on the strata argument, and its covariates differ from the recorded set.\n- The concordance of 0.640 shows modest separation of early and late arrests. The stratified concordance (0.613) counts pairs only within strata, so it is not directly comparable.\n\nWaits for you: Nothing.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n4 run_script: The script ran in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-parker-Code-guided-analysis/1838a63c-2a33-4afe-8a2a-f3a4d25b6244/scratchpad/w-rest-part-a/bench-runs/rossi1980-recidivism/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/rossi1980-recidivism/run3/home/sessions/20261012-025830-1323/work and wrote 0 new file(s) to /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-parker-Code-guided-analysis/1838a63c-2a33-4afe-8a2a-f3a4d25b6244/scratchpad/w-rest-part-a/bench-runs/rossi1980-recidivism/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/rossi1980-recidivism/run3/home/sessions/20261012-025830-1323/work.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Significance level (alpha): 0.05 · Covariates of the Cox model: fin,age,race,wexp,mar,paro,prio · Ties method of the Cox model: efron · Reference level of each categorical covariate: first.",
